  "narrative": "I am Carlos Andrés García López, a Venezuelan citizen born on November 2, 1987, in Maracaibo. I am applying for asylum because I was persecuted for my political opinion and my participation in opposition groups. In 2019, I took part in several protests against the government. After a demonstration in April 2019, I was detained for 48 hours by the national guard and beaten. I received threats and was followed on multiple occasions. I left Venezuela in July 2021, traveled through Colombia and Mexico, and entered the United States on August 14, 2021, in Miami, Florida. I have not returned to Venezuela. If I return, I fear being detained and tortured again because of my political activity. I request asylum and withholding of removal.",
